    "body": "The medium puzzle today was all about those equals constraints. I noticed a huge chain of five cells that all had to be the same value, stretching from [0,1] all the way down to [3,2]. This was the key to the whole grid. By comparing the available dominoes like [3,3] and [6,6], I realized the value had to be 6 to make the other regions work. This fixed the values for several dominoes at once, which is always a great feeling.\n\nThere were a couple of tricky spots, especially around the less than constraints at the bottom. Cell [4,1] had to be less than 2, while [4,2] had to be less than 4. I had to be careful with my remaining dominoes, [0,4] and [4,2], to ensure I didn't break those rules. I eventually placed the [0,4] domino across [3,1] and [4,1], which put a 0 in the less than 2 spot. Finishing off the [2,1] and [2,0] pairing with the [2,6] domino finally cleared the board. It definitely required a bit more jumping around the grid than the easy one did!",
